s=20
> left out, it is the default for all subsequent file-related commands unti=
l=20
> an explicit command is given, so actually:
>
> .FE %:0
> .WR:1
>
> etc. works identically.
>
> Note: When uses as files, % and $ are not actually in the TFS files=20
> directory, they are positional at the stated blocks in the beginning of t=
he=20
> tape and can save loading time when used creatively.
