> But % and $ can be used for short source file assembly by placing it in t=
o=20
> $ and the binary written to %.  In fact, there are option switches in P?S=
/8=20
> PAL that are a shorthand for the above.  But these usages are incompatibl=
e=20
> with the above ones, so let's not discuss these any further.
